[214.441597, "o", "\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0mcd /app && make 2>&1 | tail -60\r\nupcc -O -o pgen pgen.upc\r\nError during remote HTTP translation:\r\nupcc: error during UPC-to-C translation (sgiupc stage): \r\nIn file included from /usr/include/linux/stat.h:5,\r\n                 from /usr/include/aarch64-linux-gnu/bits/statx.h:31,\r\n                 from /usr/include/aarch64-linux-gnu/sys/stat.h:465,\r\n                 from /usr/local/opt/include/upcr_geninclude/sys/stat.h:14,\r\n                 from pgen.upc:22:\r\n/usr/include/linux/types.h:12: syntax error before `__s128'\r\n/usr/include/linux/types.h:13: syntax error before `__u128'\r\npgen.upc: In function `main':\r\npgen.upc:139: C99 variable length arrays not yet supported by Berkeley UPC\r\n\r\nmake: *** [Makefile:12: pgen] Error 255\r\n"]
