[933.965973, "o", "\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0mcd /app && make test && echo '=== output files ===' && ls -l serial.out pgen_*.out && echo '=== contig lengths ===' && echo 'serial:' && awk '{print length($0)}' serial.out && for f in pgen_*.out; do echo \"$f:\"; awk '{print length($0)}' \"$f\"; done\r\n./serial ./test\r\nupcrun -n 4 -shared-heap 256MB ./pgen ./test\r\nUPCR: UPC thread 0 of 4 on 91875131cfe2 (pshm node 0 of 1, process 0 of 4, pid=77192)\r\nUPCR: UPC thread 3 of 4 on 91875131cfe2 (pshm node 0 of 1, process 3 of 4, pid=77212)\r\nUPCR: UPC thread 1 of 4 on 91875131cfe2 (pshm node 0 of 1, process 1 of 4, pid=77210)\r\nUPCR: UPC thread 2 of 4 on 91875131cfe2 (pshm node 0 of 1, process 2 of 4, pid=77211)\r\ncat pgen_*.out | sort > .pgen.sorted\r\nsort serial.out > .serial.sorted\r\ndiff -u .serial.sorted .pgen.sorted\r\nrm -f .pgen.sorted .serial.sorted\r\n=== output files ===\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root  5067 Nov  1 05:18 pgen_0.out\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root  1228 Nov  1 05:18 pgen_1.out\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root     0 Nov  1 05:18 pgen_2.out\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root  3819 Nov  1 05:18 pgen_3.out\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root 10114 Nov  1 05:18 serial.out\r\n=== contig lengths ===\r\nserial:\r\n3598\r\n1467\r\n846\r\n380\r\n3590\r\n227\r\npgen_0.out:\r\n3598\r\n1467\r\npgen_1.out:\r\n846\r\n380\r\npgen_2.out:\r\npgen_3.out:\r\n3590\r\n227\r\n"]
[935.695518, "o", "> build · deepseek-v4.1-flash\r\n"]
[940.698492, "o", "Done. Both implementations are built and verified.\r\n\r\n## Deliverables in `/app`\r\n\r\n| File | Purpose |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| `serial.c` | Serial de Bruijn graph construction/traversal |\r\n| `pgen.upc` | Parallel UPC implementation |\r\n| `Makefile` | Builds `serial` and `pgen`; includes `make test` |\r\n| `README.md` | Build/run/verification notes |\r\n| `serial` | Serial executable |\r\n| `pgen` | Parallel UPC executable |\r\n| `serial.out` | Serial contigs |\r\n| `pgen_0.out` … `pgen_3.out` | Parallel contigs (per UPC thread) |\r\n\r\n## Build and run\r\n\r\n```sh\r\ncd /app\r\nmake\r\n./serial /app/test\r\nupcrun -n 4 -shared-heap 256MB /app/pgen /app/test\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Verification\r\n\r\n```sh\r\nsort serial.out > /tmp/serial.sorted\r\ncat pgen_*.out | sort > /tmp/pgen.sorted\r\ndiff -u /tmp/serial.sorted /tmp/pgen.sorted\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe comparison passes with 6 identical contigs of lengths:\r\n\r\n```\r\n3598, 1467, 846, 380, 3590, 227\r\n```\r\n\r\n`make test` also runs this verification automatically. The parallel version was validated successfully with 4, 8, 16, and 20 UPC threads.\r\n\r\nBerkeley UPC 2022.10.0 is installed under `/usr/local`, and `pgen` is linked with the SMP conduit (`upcc -O -network=smp`).\r\n"]
[940.78198, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@91875131cfe2:/app# "]
[947.524617, "i", "\u0004"]
[947.524831, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\r\n"]
[947.52508, "o", "exit\r\n"]
